<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Breaking news from AFRICA, Maghreb and Sub-Saharan Africa - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24’s coverage of events, politics and social issues across Africa, including North Africa (the Maghreb) and the Sahel, aided by our network of correspondents and experts across the continent.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/africa/rss</id><updated>2026-10-30T06:02:26Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Tunisians drawn into Russia's war in Ukraine</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d24e4299c79c5850fecd2b3284e132c28548e72c2410348a169c77c6a7bb34d6</id><updated>2026-10-30T06:02:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T21:48:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tunisians-drawn-into-russia-s-war-in-ukraine" /><summary type="html">In tonight's edition,  concern is growing in Tunisia as the families of several men who travelled to Russia for work or study are still searching for an answer about the fate of their loved ones forcibly conscripted to the war in Ukraine. Also, a year after Tanzania's controversial election, the fear hasn't faded. And Dakar is ready to make history, as the first Olympic event ever held on African soil gets underway this weekend.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Across Africa: Real estate scams growing in Ivory Coast</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7680fa90b9e78db68b3a9b3a36bde2b164763799ec6bc5ee27d3df6475ea5d10</id><updated>2026-10-30T06:02:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T21:43:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/across-africa-real-estate-scams-growing-in-ivory-coast" /><summary type="html">This week in Across Africa: in Ivory Coast, severe housing shortage has fueled demand for land, creating opportunities for fraudsters selling fake properties and non-existent plots. Also, Kenya’s women are changing the game. From the track to the boxing ring, female athletes are delivering some of the country’s biggest sporting successes. And Addis Ababa pushes ahead with ambitious plans to become East Africa’s clean-energy powerhouse.</summary><category term="Across Africa" /></entry><entry><title>DR Congo: A centre celebrates the discharge of last Ebola patients</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d078bbcbd5e2e83fcc7d5b1625a9852c866716bf92efc1204eab734bbf334a94</id><updated>2026-10-30T06:02:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T17:13:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-dr-congo-a-centre-celebrates-the-discharge-of-last-ebola-patients" /><summary type="html">Medical staff and residents at a treatment centre in Ituri danced and sang to celebrate a first since May: the centre is no longer treating any confirmed Ebola cases.</summary></entry><entry><title>Putin seeks to expand ties with African countries at Russia-Africa summit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7d04c1510388cd32d07e484f16d3a5da3b80880aa2a918dcd24e2edc51fd8dac</id><updated>2026-10-30T06:02:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T13:32:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-putin-seeks-to-expand-ties-with-african-countries-at-russia-africa-summit--7fe29c8b00d2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-putin-seeks-to-expand-ties-with-african-countries-at-russia-africa-summit" /><summary type="html">Russian President Vladimir Putin on Wednesday hosted dozens of African leaders at a Russia-Africa summit, part of Moscow’s efforts to expand its influence across the continent. The Russia-Africa summit marks a renewed Kremlin effort to bolster ties with a continent of nearly 1.6 billion people that is increasingly assertive on the global stage.</summary></entry><entry><title>DRC: C64 opposition coalition meets in Rome, calls for inclusive dialogue</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e277937842e9a381a2f04c7501ca3e2a478bdb31297f7888555afc2028a0d7af</id><updated>2026-10-30T06:02:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T13:28:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-drc-c64-opposition-coalition-meets-in-rome-calls-for-inclusive-dialogue--2673a39bc735.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-drc-c64-opposition-coalition-meets-in-rome-calls-for-inclusive-dialogue" /><summary type="html">Democratic Republic ⁠of Congo's main ​opposition coalition, C64, met in Rome on Tuesday. Under pressure to respond to Joseph Kabila’s rebellion, its five leaders addressed the situation in the country from the Italian capital. They condemned any seizure of power by force and called for inclusive dialogue. FRANCE 24’s Emmet Livingston reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Niger: Guards accused of 'cruel, inhuman' treatment after 33 die in detention</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bf0aaa83648e0821ea4caf46258415b2ab80ba396095ec25b7a276566dcb6c62</id><updated>2026-10-30T06:02:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T13:17:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-niger-guards-accused-of-cruel-inhuman-treatment-after-33-die-in-detention--06ca18f6c774.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-niger-guards-accused-of-cruel-inhuman-treatment-after-33-die-in-detention" /><summary type="html">In Niger, guards ignored the panicked cries for help from 33 detainees who died in a detention cell last month. Reports indicate that 72 people were crowded into a poorly ventilated, 20-square-metre space, where dozens slowly suffocated over 11 hours. The cell may have been cleaned and disinfected before it could be investigated. FRANCE 24's correspondent Sam Olukoya has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Kenya's female athletes make their mark as Youth Olympic Games approach</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:57901ff1cb371656501cd0b0dfb2ebea4f7fe7eda09e0afa0c148f75c11e2966</id><updated>2026-10-30T06:02:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T10:45:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-kenya-s-female-athletes-make-their-mark-as-youth-olympic-games-approach--fa8c0d0a87ff.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-kenya-s-female-athletes-make-their-mark-as-youth-olympic-games-approach" /><summary type="html">Senegal is preparing to host the Youth Olympic Games, which begin this weekend. The young athletes who hope to showcase their talents on the international stage have their sights set on the Games, and Kenya has made sure that its young boxers remain on their toes and are ready to take on opponents of a higher calibre. FRANCE 24's Bastien Renouil reports from the ground.</summary></entry><entry><title>Somalia: Lower house of parliament passes bill on sexual violence</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4a233dcb78c89e52cd24f97f0d90fcf4b5a59e506a1a2144b98fa1f2d85e20d5</id><updated>2026-10-30T06:02:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T10:42:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-somalia-lower-house-of-parliament-passes-bill-on-sexual-violence--471d5dd22da0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-somalia-lower-house-of-parliament-passes-bill-on-sexual-violence" /><summary type="html">The Somali Parliament has passed a new law against sexual violence. The country’s criminal code dated back to 1962 and had not been updated since. FRANCE 24's Bastien Renouil met with Sofia Rajab in Nairobi. She is the program manager at the NGO Legal Action Worldwide, an organisation that lobbied Somali authorities in support of this new law.</summary></entry><entry><title>Russia woos African leaders at Moscow summit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1669d833f54946638bf3ac1839424fdf248cb374a12bd92cb7ee0992a287fcd5</id><updated>2026-10-30T06:02:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T21:27:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/russia-woos-african-leaders-at-moscow-summit--0fad5419a542.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/russia-woos-african-leaders-at-moscow-summit" /><summary type="html">In tonight's edition: A summit with nearly two dozen African leaders opens in Moscow, with the Kremlin describing their countries as natural allies against the West. Also, Nigerian investigators say that dozens of detained miners who died in a crowded jail cell screamed for help as jailors ignored their suffering. And ahead of the Youth Olympics in Senegal, Kenya is ramping up support for its female athletes.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Putin woos African leaders as Moscow seeks to expand footprint in Africa</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4a875e04abb120986828f8b8b9c9f5be5ef2c55b51ba81ec39335d6e59be64eb</id><updated>2026-10-30T06:02:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T18:13:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20261028-putin-woos-african-leaders-moscow-seeks-expand-footprint-africa--1f573b05cce8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261028-putin-woos-african-leaders-moscow-seeks-expand-footprint-africa" /><summary type="html">Russian President Vladimir Putin sought to woo African leaders and government delegates on Wednesday as they gathered in Moscow for the third Russia-Africa Summit to discuss trade, security, arms deals and grain supplies as part of the Kremlin's strategic efforts to expand its footprint in Africa.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Ethiopia clashes push 50,000 to flee to Kenya</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e0ada4431bcce8521d24a0b26219b987f26e08a313ca4605fb1b4bc9ee0b3c4e</id><updated>2026-10-30T06:02:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T16:29:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20261028-ethiopia-clashes-push-50-000-flee-to-kenya--d0b352552396.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261028-ethiopia-clashes-push-50-000-flee-to-kenya" /><summary type="html">The outbreak of fighting between rival forces in southern Ethiopia last week has led some 50,000 people to seek refuge in neighbouring Kenya, the United Nations said Wednesday, citing local authorities.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Africa's Ebola outbreak tops 10,000 cases, mainly in DR Congo</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:45f7be3481c0a9402fcc09fa34a5fd99e14e8ce0cadcc1df6b16c50a6c89d6a3</id><updated>2026-10-30T06:02:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T15:45:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20261027-africa-ebola-outbreak-tops-10-000-cases-mainly-dr-congo--4e6edb8c38f5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261027-africa-ebola-outbreak-tops-10-000-cases-mainly-dr-congo" /><summary type="html">Africa's outbreak of the Ebola virus has passed more than 10,000 cases, health authorities said Tuesday, with the vast majority located in Democratic Republic of Congo. There are currently no approved vaccines for the rare Bundibugyo species of Ebola driving the current infections.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Sudan: One year after the fall of El-Fasher</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9ebab9d0844292ecfe4adb8b14b5eeef75d22cf507e2a1db1a974380b2fa79cb</id><updated>2026-10-30T06:02:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T11:46:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261027-sudan-one-year-after-the-fall-of-el-fasher--874d8fa8f1e9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261027-sudan-one-year-after-the-fall-of-el-fasher" /><summary type="html">It has been one year since the fall of El-Fasher in Sudan, a city in North Darfur, which was captured by the Rapid Support Forces. At least 6,000 civilians were killed by rebel troops as they entered this strategic city.</summary></entry><entry><title>South Africa suspends asylum applications after recent unrest</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:28c76d9eb3a3341938948570d668dfbc2c933d638a4e98b0a987d608c67a1bd1</id><updated>2026-10-30T06:02:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T11:37:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261027-south-africa-suspends-asylum-applications-after-recent-unrest--7a8cca00906a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261027-south-africa-suspends-asylum-applications-after-recent-unrest" /><summary type="html">Tensions in South Africa over anti-migrant protests have left in limbo many who were counting on following the rules to sort out their paperwork and status in the country. Calls for a crackdown on foreigners, particularly undocumented migrants, have sometimes spiralled into murder. In response to the unrest, the government suspended the asylum application process.</summary></entry><entry><title>Algeria to deploy army units to Niger to protect economic interests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8f8048bbc95d6b883645d75f3da7850da44966c4e6e6b56ee47ff30acca9a992</id><updated>2026-10-30T06:02:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T11:28:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261027-algeria-deploys-army-units-to-niger-to-protect-economic-interests--dda1a7fe9e79.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261027-algeria-deploys-army-units-to-niger-to-protect-economic-interests" /><summary type="html">Algeria will send army units to Niger to ​protect energy and economic interests, according to a statement from the presidency on Monday (October 26). Algeria's Parliament held an emergency vote on Sunday on what would be Algeria's first such foreign mission since 1973.</summary></entry><entry><title>Chad hosts hundreds of thousands of Sudanese refugees as regional humanitarian crisis extends</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dbf592c7c74f85478a9377861ac9089f543ce4ef0b461be895cafcabe8a5d653</id><updated>2026-10-30T06:02:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T11:13:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261027-chad-hosts-hundreds-of-thousands-of-sudanese-refugees-as-regional-humanitarian-crisis-exten--ea71b37e071c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261027-chad-hosts-hundreds-of-thousands-of-sudanese-refugees-as-regional-humanitarian-crisis-extends" /><summary type="html">Sudan’s war is spilling over into Chad. A drone strike killed at least four people last week in the border town of Bamina, and hundreds of thousands of Sudanese refugees have crossed over in search of safety. Many of those who survived the massacre in El Fasher are still deeply traumatised. FRANCE 24's correspondent Harold Girard has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>The fall of Sudan's El-Fasher, one year on</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d11b5fc92914f30463c39dbf0758af3c08720e5f7be3bc95ea5e6774f1df8601</id><updated>2026-10-30T06:02:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T21:26:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/the-fall-of-el-fasher-one-year-on--b474e4157040.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/the-fall-of-el-fasher-one-year-on" /><summary type="html">In tonight's edition: 15 military officials in Sudan are sanctioned by the UK over the brutality and abuse of civilians during the fall of El-Fasher. Also, ⁠Algeria is set to send in army units ​to ‌Niger ⁠to ‌protect energy ⁠and economic interests there. And days after a foreigner was beaten to death on the streets of Durban, the stalled asylum process has left many migrants in South Africa living in fear.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Algeria to send troops to Niger in first foreign deployment in over 50 years</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:663ac27809dc2e126511ac29bb395b36d96a5899be8efe50cd4ef7124eb0ad11</id><updated>2026-10-30T06:02:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T10:10:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20261026-algeria-to-send-troops-to-niger-in-first-foreign-deployment-in-over-50-years--5abdc8f17645.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261026-algeria-to-send-troops-to-niger-in-first-foreign-deployment-in-over-50-years" /><summary type="html">Algeria’s parliament on Sunday approved a resolution to send troops to Niger, making the first time Algerian soldiers will be deployed abroad since the 1973 Arab-Israeli war. Niger faces persistent attacks by armed groups, including near its border with Algeria, and the deployment comes as Algiers and Niamey are building the Trans-Saharan Gas Pipeline after decades of delays.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Building collapse in Nairobi: Search for survivors under way</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b23a50deb1d36133a85ed9d26da49db2c109f6d929c1beb4cad5b2044fa049f9</id><updated>2026-10-30T06:02:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T20:31:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/building-collapse-in-nairobi-search-for-survivors-under-way--5d7e9d1e7359.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/building-collapse-in-nairobi-search-for-survivors-under-way" /><summary type="html">In tonight's programme: Rescuers comb through rubble in a bid to reach trapped survivors after a multi-storey building under construction in Nairobi collapses. Also, Kenya announces a second Ebola death. Earlier this week it had logged nine cases, all traced back to its first Ebola patient who died earlier this month. Finally, with the 11th edition of the iconic contemporary art festival Also Known as Africa taking place in Paris, we speak to Cape Verdean artist Amadeo Carvalho.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>SA faces rising tension as foreign national is killed amid anti-migrant protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e43a53be89d04217fecab64e60440234a3a28e47385403d39c1e7103ea4ec7a2</id><updated>2026-10-30T06:02:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T11:08:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/sa-faces-rising-tension-as-foreign-national-is-killed-amid-anti-migrant-protests--97fdf43717d9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/sa-faces-rising-tension-as-foreign-national-is-killed-amid-anti-migrant-protests" /><summary type="html">South African police are investigating the murder of a foreign national after violent protests by anti-immigrant groups swept through the central business district in Durban. The latest death follows months of violent rallies in which at least 10 foreigners were killed and several other countries on the continent raced to repatriate their people. Details by FRANCE 24's correspondent Eunice Masson.</summary></entry><entry><title>Across Africa: Ivorian vinyl head's heritage hunt</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:809bec7e56e246543549666c9dfbf20d948fc1550b23ff1ff9286e5b32950b4a</id><updated>2026-10-30T06:02:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T10:27:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/across-africa/20261023-across-africa-ivorian-vinyl-head-s-heritage-hunt--b506a2325208.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/across-africa/20261023-across-africa-ivorian-vinyl-head-s-heritage-hunt" /><summary type="html">This week in Across Africa: Ivorian music lover Cédric Kouamé is on a mission to restore 20th-century African vinyl and bring old-school sounds back to modern playlists. Also, 10 years after Cameroon's worst railway disaster, families are still fighting for justice for the 79 people killed. Finally, in São Tomé and Príncipe, we discover how the islands' rich volcanic soils produce some of the world's most distinctive vanilla.</summary><category term="Across Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Olympic fever grips Senegal as Dakar hosts Youth Olympic Games</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fbaf4f3d54aaa94a1f17a700bd2ab1d7282ade3059699cf467ae1b4a903f2db7</id><updated>2026-10-30T06:02:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T09:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/reporters/20261023-olympic-fever-grips-senegal-as-dakar-hosts-youth-olympic-games-yog--8929ff69c2de.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/reporters/20261023-olympic-fever-grips-senegal-as-dakar-hosts-youth-olympic-games-yog" /><summary type="html">As Senegal prepares to host the Youth Olympic Games (YOG), the first Olympic event ever organised in Africa, the country is pulling out all the stops to be ready on time. FRANCE 24’s Sarah Sakho and Simon Martin report.</summary><category term="Reporters" /></entry><entry><title>Ivory Coast: Children face serious health risks from lead in paint</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4968bbc8292d1c841719860b7e67a0ad95095635b98d5dd8306a9f3b69940564</id><updated>2026-10-30T06:02:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T08:37:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/ivory-coast-children-face-serious-health-risks-from-lead-in-paint--1797f4fd2521.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ivory-coast-children-face-serious-health-risks-from-lead-in-paint" /><summary type="html">Across Ivory Coast, teams are going door-to-door, testing homes for dangerous levels of lead as efforts to raise awareness of the toxic metal’s health risks intensify. Report by Jean Barrère &amp; Guillaume Gougeon.</summary></entry><entry><title>Africa faces 'complex' Ebola outbreak after spread to Nigeria: WHO</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:21884371ae073b54c2ae79a7a0440e5f927af84382f736479c43529b521103cf</id><updated>2026-10-30T06:02:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T08:28:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa-faces-complex-ebola-outbreak-after-spread-to-nigeria-who--e04938ba7420.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa-faces-complex-ebola-outbreak-after-spread-to-nigeria-who" /><summary type="html">The World Health Organization warned Thursday that Africa faced a "complex" Ebola outbreak after the virus crossed from east Africa to Nigeria, marking the first case in the west of the continent.</summary></entry><entry><title>South Africa gripped by anti-migrant protests as foreign national is killed</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f74bc625e9305b64e6e8f38e7224f088d33e4f948bf35430d1384e6ac83a13ef</id><updated>2026-10-30T06:02:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T08:24:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/eye-on-africa/20261023-south-africa-gripped-by-anti-migrant-protests-as-foreign-national-is-killed--ea4014e7134c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/eye-on-africa/20261023-south-africa-gripped-by-anti-migrant-protests-as-foreign-national-is-killed" /><summary type="html">Xenophobic unrest turns deadly in South Africa as a foreign national is beaten to death during a protest march in Durban, a city increasingly gripped by anti-migrant tensions. Meanwhile, as global efforts to raise awareness of lead poisoning intensify, teams in Ivory Coast go door-to-door testing homes for dangerous levels of the toxic metal. Finally, Ivorian authorities are cracking down on illegal mining over fears of pollution, but some young people say the activity remains one of their few sources of income.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Ethiopia-Eritrea: Is there a risk of a wider conflict?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7f8a4704c1e3efcc1fa5e023536e953e9c8c21e1d8052972cadcc55c22225947</id><updated>2026-10-30T06:02:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T15:40:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20261022-ethiopia-eritrea-is-there-a-risk-of-a-wider-conflict--3f21072314d8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20261022-ethiopia-eritrea-is-there-a-risk-of-a-wider-conflict" /><summary type="html">Concerns are mounting as Ethiopia and Eritrea inch closer to war. With Ethiopia now having taken control of the border town of Zalambessa, the fear is that Prime Minister Abiy Ahmed will send his troops into Eritrea. In Perspective, we spoke to Martin Plaut, a senior research fellow at the Institute of Commonwealth Studies at the University of London.</summary><category term="Perspective" /></entry><entry><title>Cameroon: Ten years after a massive train disaster, victims are still awaiting justice</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3782eac0557dde0a42fa71d38fa0d0f4421782731f70122e3e9951faf53e1f16</id><updated>2026-10-30T06:02:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T14:23:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261022-cameroon-ten-years-after-a-massive-train-disaster-victims-are-still-awaiting-justice--8e557c9796f5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261022-cameroon-ten-years-after-a-massive-train-disaster-victims-are-still-awaiting-justice" /><summary type="html">It has been ten years since a Cameroon National Railway Intercity train travelling between Yaounde and Douala derailed and became the country's worst ever railway disaster. Seventy-nine people were killed and hundreds were injured. Report by Indira Ayuk, Richard Tessoh, Giresse Ngaana &amp; Guillaume Gougeon.</summary></entry><entry><title>Sudan's war escalates as UN warns of wider regional crisis</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6744929ec0d173284286b11f2a77c7ef341b61d747916d84f32b29f491af9cc0</id><updated>2026-10-30T06:02:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T22:41:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/eye-on-africa/20261021-sudan-s-war-escalates-as-un-warns-of-wider-regional-crisis--064ccd824912.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/eye-on-africa/20261021-sudan-s-war-escalates-as-un-warns-of-wider-regional-crisis" /><summary type="html">In tonight's edition: Sudan's brutal war continues to take a devastating regional toll, as a drone strike in Abyei reportedly kills 153 people. We speak to the UN envoy for Sudan following an emergency international meeting on the escalating crisis. Also, health authorities prepare to coordinate a response as Ebola cases emerge in Nigeria and rise in Kenya. Finally, 10 years after Cameroon’s deadliest railway disaster, families of the 79 victims are still fighting for justice, saying their pain has yet to be acknowledged.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>'Neither the Sudanese military, nor the RSF take any acknowledgement of human life in this war'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f41dfd3f14a1ecf097d09af0d0bf6a793a09ebfa4416e26f0774fa6be3e7ab6d</id><updated>2026-10-30T06:02:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T19:28:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/neither-the-sudanese-military-nor-the-rsf-take-any-acknowledgement-of-human-life-in-this-war--7a1f83fdb2cf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/neither-the-sudanese-military-nor-the-rsf-take-any-acknowledgement-of-human-life-in-this-war" /><summary type="html">The death toll from a drone strike Monday on a market in an area disputed between Sudan and South Sudan has risen to 153 and is likely even higher, a local official told AFP on Wednesday. Authorities in Abyei district said the strike on the Amiet market involved the use of multiple munitions and was carried out by the Sudanese army. FRANCE 24's Mark Owen speaks with Jan Pospisil, Sudan Affairs Analyst at the Peace and Conflict Resolution Evidence Platform. He says that for a long time the Sudanese army has tried "to portray a picture internationally that they are humane, whereas RSF is committing atrocities. Here we see very clearly that there is not much difference between these two".</summary></entry><entry><title>Kenya: Trial shows crucial role of religion in Shakahola massacre</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4598cdf72b5600e2778d9c3355e51efe46cac8066e4fba6256cb3ad27ef7ec54</id><updated>2026-10-30T06:02:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T13:48:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261021-kenya-trial-shows-crucial-role-of-religion-in-shakahola-massacre--eb311fee9b1e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261021-kenya-trial-shows-crucial-role-of-religion-in-shakahola-massacre" /><summary type="html">The Kenyan cult leader found guilty on Monday of the deaths of 190 children and one adult will be sentenced on November 6th. Paul Mackenzie starved his followers in what became known as the Shakahola massacre. But this trial was about more than just a criminal and his accomplices. Details by FRANCE 24's correspondent Bastien Renouil.</summary></entry></feed>
